# Architecture Rules

## Canonical Folder Structure
```
src/
  app/                          ← Next.js App Router (route segments, layouts, API routes)
    (dashboard)/                ← authenticated shell with DesktopNav + TabBar
      layout.tsx
      page.tsx                  ← Home
      search/[query]/page.tsx
      product/[id]/page.tsx
      cabs/page.tsx
      watchlist/page.tsx
    api/
      prices/{grocery,electronics,cabs}/route.ts
      search/trending/route.ts
      alerts/route.ts
      watchlist/route.ts
      history/[productId]/route.ts
      cron/check-alerts/route.ts
    layout.tsx                  ← root: fonts, ThemeProvider, globals
    globals.css
  components/
    ui/                         ← GlassCard, SearchBar, ResultCard, VerdictChip, badges
    layout/                     ← DesktopNav, TabBar
    features/                   ← SparkChart, PlatformLogo, PriceAlert, WatchlistButton
  lib/
    scrapers/                   ← BaseScraper + per-platform scrapers (Railway only)
    cache/redis.ts              ← Upstash client + key factories
    db/supabase.ts              ← Supabase client + query utilities
    ai/verdict.ts               ← rule-based + optional LLM verdict engine
    geo/index.ts                ← city detection from request headers
    utils/
      format.ts                 ← formatPrice, formatRelativeTime, normalizeQuery
      platforms.ts              ← PLATFORMS registry (single source of truth)
  styles/
    tokens.css                  ← all CSS variables — the only place colors/spacing/radius live
  types/
    index.ts                    ← all shared types, single barrel export
```

## Dependency Direction
- `src/app/` imports from `src/components/` and `src/lib/` only.
- `src/components/features/` imports from `src/components/ui/`, `src/lib/utils/`, `src/types/`.
- `src/components/ui/` must not import from `src/components/features/` or `src/lib/scrapers/`.
- `src/lib/` modules must not import from `src/components/` or `src/app/`.
- `src/types/index.ts` has no internal imports — pure type declarations only.
- Circular imports are never acceptable.

## Server vs Client Boundary
- Server Components are the default for all pages, layouts, and data-fetching components.
- Add `"use client"` only for: search input interactivity, tab/nav active state, charts (Canvas), theme toggle, SWR hooks, optimistic watchlist/alert mutations, live time counters.
- Every async Server Component that fetches data must have a Suspense boundary with a matching skeleton component.

## Scraper Isolation
- Scraper modules (`src/lib/scrapers/`) run exclusively on the Railway service.
- Next.js API routes call the Railway scraper service via HTTP — they never import `playwright` or run browser automation directly.
- The Railway service is the only place Playwright is installed or executed.

## Import Conventions
- Use `@/*` alias (mapped to `src/*`) for all non-relative imports.
- Relative imports are allowed only within the same immediate folder.
- Import from `src/types/index.ts` barrel, not from individual type files.
